It seems like you are dealing with a build error or import statement related to a Vue.js component, which is using Less for its styles and attempting to chain a number of Webpack loaders together to process those styles.

The error message is suggesting that you have encountered a module resolution problem or missing dependency related to the styles of the `Dashboard.vue` component.

However, the suggested command to install the missing loaders is not formatted correctly. You shouldn't copy the whole error string into the `npm install` command.

Instead, you should ensure that you have all necessary loaders installed as devDependencies in your project. To do so, run the following npm commands:

```shell
npm install --save-dev vue-style-loader css-loader less-loader
```

Make sure that you have the `vue-loader` installed as well since you are working with Vue components:

```shell
npm install --save-dev vue-loader
```

Once you've installed these packages, make sure your Webpack configuration is set up correctly to handle `.vue` files and to use the loaders for the styles. You should have rules similar to the following in your webpack.config.js (exact configuration may vary depending on your build setup and Webpack version):

```js
module.exports = {
  // ...
  module: {
    rules: [
      {
        test: /\.vue$/,
        loader: 'vue-loader'
      },
      {
        test: /\.css$/,
        use: [
          'vue-style-loader',
          'css-loader'
        ]
      },
      {
        test: /\.less$/,
        use: [
          'vue-style-loader',
          'css-loader',
          'less-loader'
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  // ...
};
```

By setting up your Webpack configuration with these rules, it should be able to handle the import and processing of styles within your Vue components. Remember to restart your build process after making these changes.

